<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: DETAILS OF CZECH FOREIGN TRADE BALANCE FOR 1996.</title>
<headline>DETAILS OF CZECH FOREIGN TRADE BALANCE FOR 1996.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of Czech foreign trade figures for the year 1996, as published by the Czech Statistical Bureau on Monday.</p>
<p>  (JANUARY-DEC PERIOD)	 imports     exports     balance</p>
<p>BY TERRITORY (in billions of crowns) Countries with a</p>
<p>  developed market economy    530.894     378.149    -152.745</p>
<p>   of that: EU countries	470.956     345.992    -124.964</p>
<p>  Developing countries	   37.862	33.179	-4.683</p>
<p>European countries with transitional economy, and</p>
<p>  CIS countries		   177.376     180.343	 2.967</p>
<p>Other countries with transitional or state</p>
<p>  economies			   8.669	 2.711	-5.958</p>
<p>  Unspecified countries	   0.477	 0.570	 0.093</p>
<p>  Total			     755.278     594.952    -160.326</p>
<p>   of that: OECD countries    535.382     377.763    -157.619</p>
<p>BY PRODUCT GROUPS (in billions of crowns)</p>
<p>Agricultural products</p>
<p>  and foodstuffs		 52.005	  31.094   -20.911</p>
<p>Raw materials, unprocessed goods</p>
<p>  and chemical products     327.879	 280.571   -47.308</p>
<p>Machinery and</p>
<p>  transport equipment	 288.492	 194.572   -93.920</p>
<p>Industrial consumer</p>
<p>  products			 86.902	  88.715     1.813</p>
<p>  Total			   755.278	 594.952  -160.326</p>
<p>  Total index 1996/95 (pct) 112.7	   103.5</p>
<p>Note. All figures in billions of crowns on customs-cleared basis and subject to revision.</p>
<p>-- Alan Crosby, Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
